        <briefdescription>
<para>A counterpart of LiveRange::createDeadDef: Make sure the range has a value defined at <computeroutput>Def</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>If <computeroutput>ForVNI</computeroutput> is null, and there is no value defined at <computeroutput>Def</computeroutput>, a new value will be allocated using <computeroutput>VNInfoAllocator</computeroutput>. If <computeroutput>ForVNI</computeroutput> is null, the return value is the value defined at <computeroutput>Def</computeroutput>, either a pre-existing one, or the one newly created. If <computeroutput>ForVNI</computeroutput> is not null, then <computeroutput>Def</computeroutput> should be the location where <computeroutput>ForVNI</computeroutput> is defined. If the range does not have a value defined at <computeroutput>Def</computeroutput>, the value <computeroutput>ForVNI</computeroutput> will be used instead of allocating a new one. If the range already has a value defined at <computeroutput>Def</computeroutput>, it must be same as <computeroutput>ForVNI</computeroutput>. In either case, <computeroutput>ForVNI</computeroutput> will be the return value. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
